  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "A shopper buys a \\(\\$100\\) coat on sale for \\(20\\%\\) off. An additional \\(\\$5\\) is taken off the sale price by using a discount coupon. A sales tax of \\(8\\%\\) is paid on the final selling price. The total amount the shopper pays for the coat is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$81.00\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$81.40\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$82.00\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$82.08\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$82.40\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A \\(20\\%\\) discount means the shopper pays \\(80\\%\\) of the original price. The sale price is therefore\n\\[\n100\\times 0.80=80\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThe coupon then reduces the selling price to \\(80-5=75\\) dollars. Since the tax is charged on this final selling price, the tax is\n\\[\n75\\times 0.08=6\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThe total payment is \\(75+6=\\boxed{\\$81.00}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
